<mxCell id="lgt3" value="External / referenced-only table (users, or any owning module&#39;s row)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;fontColor=#12181F;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="72" y="525" width="620" height="24" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="fn1" value="field_values.field_def_id and field_values.entity_id are deliberately NOT foreign keys (dashed edges above): the target table for entity_id varies by entity_type, so the link is app-enforced, not DB-enforced — the same discipline used platform-wide for subject_type/subject_id pointers. Do not confuse entity_type with that subject_type/subject_id pattern, though: entity_type is a registration key an owning module chooses for its OWN record type (e.g. legal_case, inventory_item), resolved entirely inside that module&#39;s own Service layer — it never points at a different module&#39;s record the way subject_type/subject_id does (§5). field_def_audit_logs.field_def_id and .actor_id are real, DB-enforced foreign keys (solid edges) — field definitions are never hard-deleted, so referencing them safely is possible." style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontColor=#4A5563;align=left;fontStyle=2;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="574" width="1340" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
